==========================================
NETWORKING DAY 01 NOTES — ping, traceroute & mtr
Date: 29-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- ping sends ICMP echo requests; shows reachability, latency (time=) and packet loss
- TTL drops by 1 at every router; starting values ~64 (Linux), 128 (Windows), 255 (devices)
- traceroute uses increasing TTL to reveal each router along the path
- mtr = ping + traceroute, with loss % and latency per hop
- ping by IP works but by name fails -> DNS problem, not connectivity
- "* * *" in traceroute = hop didn't reply (often just blocked)
- Loss at a middle hop but 0% at the final hop is usually ICMP rate limiting

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] ping -c 4 127.0.0.1
[ ] ip route | grep default  +  ping gateway
[ ] ping -c 4 8.8.8.8  /  ping -c 4 google.com
[ ] ping -c 3 -W 1 192.0.2.1  (deliberate failure)
[ ] traceroute -n 8.8.8.8
[ ] mtr -r -c 10 google.com

